ps://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-oss/\", \"https://huggingface.co/openai/gpt-oss-120b/raw/main/README.md\"], \"provider\": \"OpenAI\", \"relation\": \"pretrained\", \"extensions\": {\"notes\": \"The released checkpoint is described as trained from scratch through pretraining followed by post-training, but no separate public pretrained parent checkpoint is identified. The training corpus and detailed post-training data are not individually disclosed.\", \"disclosure_status\": \"partially_disclosed\"}}, \"safety_ethics\": {\"extensions\": {\"risk_summary\": \"The model includes safety training and filtering, but its open weights can be modified to bypass refusals or increase harmful capabilities, so downstream deployers must add safeguards and monitoring.\"}, \"mitigation\": [{\"reference\": \"https://cdn.openai.com/pdf/419b6906-9da6-406c-a19d-1bb078ac7637/oai_gpt-oss_model_card.pdf\", \"description\": \"Pretraining data was filtered for harmful content, especially hazardous CBRN-related content, using CBRN filters from GPT-4o.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://cdn.openai.com/pdf/419b6906-9da6-406c-a19d-1bb078ac7637/oai_gpt-oss_model_card.pdf\", \"description\": \"Post-training used deliberative alignment and instruction hierarchy training to encourage refusal of unsafe prompts and resistance to prompt injection.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://openai.com/index/gpt-oss-model-card/\", \"description\": \"OpenAI recommends additional downstream safeguards, filtering, moderation, monitoring, or summarization, especially before exposing chain-of-thought to users.\"}], \"safety_risk\": [{\"reference\": \"https://openai.com/index/gpt-oss-model-card/\", \"description\": \"Open-weight release removes OpenAI\'s ability to revoke access or apply additional centralized mitigations after release; determined actors may fine-tune the model to bypass safety refusals or increase harmful capabilities.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://cdn.openai.com/pdf/419b6906-9da6-406c-a19d-1bb078ac7637/