g/abs/2508.10925\"}, \"configuration\": {\"notes\": \"Disambiguated questions.\", \"benchmark\": \"BBQ\"}}], \"provenance\": {\"origin\": \"gpt-oss\", \"evidence\": [\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"https://cdn.openai.com/pdf/419b6906-9da6-406c-a19d-1bb078ac7637/oai_gpt-oss_model_card.pdf\"], \"provider\": \"OpenAI\", \"relation\": \"pretrained\", \"extensions\": {\"notes\": \"The model card describes pretraining followed by large-scale distillation and reinforcement-learning-based post-training, but does not identify a technical parent checkpoint or the distillation teacher models.\", \"disclosure_status\": \"partially_disclosed\"}}, \"safety_ethics\": {\"extensions\": {\"risk_summary\": \"The model is safety-trained and did not reach OpenAI\'s indicative High capability thresholds in the reported Preparedness categories, but its open weights can be modified by downstream actors and deployment requires additional safeguards.\"}, \"mitigation\": [{\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"Pretraining data was filtered for harmful CBRN-related content using filters reused from GPT-4o.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"Deliberative alignment was used during post-training to teach refusal behavior and robustness to jailbreaks.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"The instruction hierarchy was used to resolve instruction conflicts and defend against prompt injection.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"OpenAI conducted scalable Preparedness evaluations and adversarial fine-tuning tests for biological, chemical, cyber, and AI self-improvement risks.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"The model card recommends downstream filtering, moderation, or summarization before exposing chain-of-thought content to users.\"}], \"safety_risk\": [{\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"Open-weight users may fine-tune the model to bypass safety refusals or optimize harmful capabilities.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"The model can hallucinate, including in factual answers and chains of thought.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"Unfiltered chains of thought may contain hallucinated content or language inconsistent with OpenAI safety policies.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"The model\'s health outputs should not be treated as professional diagnosis or treatment advice.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"The open-weight release creates a risk that downstream modifications alter the model\'s safety and capability profile.\"}], \"prohibited_use\": [{\"reference\": \"https://github.com/openai/gpt-oss/blob/main/USAGE_POLICY\", \"description\": \"Users must comply with all applicable law when using gpt-oss-120b and gpt-oss-20b.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"The model is not intended to provide medical diagnosis or treatment.\"}], \"ethical_considerations\": [{\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"Developers and enterprises may need safeguards beyond the model\'s default behavior to replicate system-level protections of hosted models.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"Chains of thought should not be shown directly to end users without additional filtering, moderation, or summarization.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"The model was evaluated for fairness and bias using BBQ, with separate ambiguous and disambiguated-question results.\"}]}, \"license_policy\": [{\"license\": \"Apache License 2.0\", \"extensions\": {\"kind\": \"declared\", \"source\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", 